======================================================================
DETAILED ANALYSIS
======================================================================

1. EMT Performance:
   • C-H Bond Length:  1.1515 Å  (error: 5.93%)
   • C-H Bond Energy:  3.2539 eV (error: 28.49%)
   • EMT severely underestimates the C-H bond energy and may give incorrect bond length
   • This is expected - EMT is a simple effective medium theory not suited for covalent bonds

2. MACE Performance:
   • C-H Bond Length:  1.0931 Å  (error: 0.56%)
   • C-H Bond Energy:  4.3158 eV (error: 5.15%)
   • MACE gives much better agreement with experiment
   • The bond length is particularly accurate

3. Method Comparison:
   ✓ MACE gives better bond length (0.0061 Å vs 0.0645 Å)
   ✓ MACE gives better bond energy (0.2342 eV vs 1.2961 eV)

4. Key Insights:
   • EMT overestimates the C-H bond length by 0.0645 Å

   • EMT underestimates the C-H bond energy by 1.2961 eV
     The bond is too weak in EMT because the potential is too soft.

   • MACE, being trained on accurate DFT data, captures the
     correct potential energy surface and gives much better results.

5. Why MACE is better for this system:
   • Methane is an organic molecule with covalent C-H bonds
   • EMT was designed for metals and simple systems
   • MACE was trained on diverse molecular datasets including organics
   • The machine-learned potential captures many-body effects
   • MACE can describe the subtle electronic structure of C-H bonds

